Implement the following plan:

# Fix PDF Text Search Highlighting Accuracy

## Problem

`packages/web/src/routes/+page.svelte` line 137:
```typescript
const charWidth = item.width / item.str.length;
```
This assumes monospace spacing. Proportional fonts have variable character widths, so highlight x-offsets accumulate error for any character not at the start of a text item. Words mid-sentence or mid-line are misaligned.

## Root Cause vs. Correct Approach

| Current (broken) | PDF.js reference approach |
|---|---|
| Calculate overlay div positions from transform matrices + monospace estimate | Inject `<span class="highlight">` inline inside already-positioned TextLayer spans |
| Coordinate math required | No coordinate math — the outer span is already pixel-perfect |
| `.search-highlight-overlay` divs appended to pageWrapper | DOM manipulation of `textDivs[i]` directly |

## Key Discovery

`TextLayer` (pdfjs-dist) exposes **two public getters** after `await textLayer.render()`:
- `textLayer.textDivs`: `HTMLElement[]` — one span per text item, already positioned
- `textLayer.textContentItemsStr`: `string[]` — text strings, 1:1 aligned with textDivs

`pdf_viewer.css` (already imported at line 2) provides ready-made CSS classes:
- `.textLayer .highlight` — background highlight (override color via `--highlight-bg-color`)
- `.textLayer .highlight.selected` — current match (override via `--highlight-selected-bg-color`)

## Only File to Modify

`/Users/daishokomiyama/Code/pdf-splitter/packages/web/src/routes/+page.svelte`

---

## Implementation Steps

### 1. Update `PageTextData` interface (lines 29–38)

```typescript
interface PageTextData {
    pageWrapper: HTMLElement;
    viewport: { width: number; height: number; scale: number };
    textDivs: HTMLElement[];         // from textLayer.textDivs after render
    textContentItemsStr: string[];   // from textLayer.textContentItemsStr after render
}
```

Remove the old `textItems` array entirely.

### 2. Update `handleFileChange` — collect TextLayer data (lines 322–348)

Change order: render text layer first, then snapshot its data:

```typescript
const textLayer = new pdfjs.TextLayer({
    textContentSource: textContent,
    container: textLayerDiv,
    viewport: viewport
});
await textLayer.render();  // Must await before reading textDivs
pageWrapper.appendChild(textLayerDiv);

pagesData.push({
    pageWrapper,
    viewport: { width: viewport.width, height: viewport.height, scale: viewport.scale },
    textDivs: Array.from(textLayer.textDivs),
    textContentItemsStr: Array.from(textLayer.textContentItemsStr)
});
```

Remove the `textContent.items` filter/map for `textItems` — no longer needed.

### 3. Add helper functions (before `performSearch`)

```typescript
// Mirrors TextHighlighter's clearDiv — restore a div to plain text
function restoreDiv(div: HTMLElement, originalText: string) {
    div.textContent = originalText;
    div.className = '';
}

// Clear a div and prepend text up to `upToOffset` as a text node
function beginDiv(div: HTMLElement, text: string, upToOffset: number) {
    div.textContent = '';
    if (upToOffset > 0) div.append(document.createTextNode(text.substring(0, upToOffset)));
}

// Append a plain text node for range [from, to)
function appendTextToDiv(div: HTMLElement, text: string, from: number, to: number) {
    if (from >= to) return;
    div.append(document.createTextNode(text.substring(from, to)));
}
```

### 4. Rewrite `performSearch` (lines 51–164)

Replace entirely:

```typescript
function performSearch() {
    // --- Clear previous highlights ---
    for (const pageData of pagesData) {
        pageData.textDivs.forEach((div, i) => restoreDiv(div, pageData.textContentItemsStr[i]));
    }
    highlightElements = [];
    matchCount = 0;
    currentMatchIndex = 0;

    if (!searchQuery.trim() || pagesData.length === 0) return;

    const query = matchCase ? searchQuery : searchQuery.toLowerCase();

    pagesData.forEach((pageData) => {
        const { textDivs, textContentItemsStr } = pageData;

        // Build charMap: charMap[absoluteIdx] = {divIdx, offset}
        interface CharPos { divIdx: number; offset: number; }
        const charMap: CharPos[] = [];
        let combinedText = '';
        for (let d = 0; d < textContentItemsStr.length; d++) {
            const s = textContentItemsStr[d];
            for (let o = 0; o < s.length; o++) charMap.push({ divIdx: d, offset: o });
            combinedText += s;
        }

        const textToSearch = matchCase ? combinedText : combinedText.toLowerCase();
        let searchPos = 0;

        // Collect converted matches: {begin, end (exclusive), matchIdx}
        interface ConvertedMatch { begin: CharPos; end: CharPos; matchIdx: number; }
        const convertedMatches: ConvertedMatch[] = [];

        while (true) {
            const matchStart = textToSearch.indexOf(query, searchPos);
            if (matchStart === -1) break;

            if (matchWholeWord) {
                const before = matchStart > 0 ? textToSearch[matchStart - 1] : ' ';
                const after = matchStart + query.length < textToSearch.length
                    ? textToSearch[matchStart + query.length] : ' ';
                if (/\w/.test(before) || /\w/.test(after)) { searchPos = matchStart + 1; continue; }
            }

            const endIdx = matchStart + query.length - 1;
            if (charMap[matchStart] && charMap[endIdx]) {
                convertedMatches.push({
                    begin: charMap[matchStart],
                    end: { divIdx: charMap[endIdx].divIdx, offset: charMap[endIdx].offset + 1 },
                    matchIdx: matchCount++
                });
            }
            searchPos = matchStart + 1;
        }

        if (convertedMatches.length === 0) return;

        // Render matches into DOM (mirrors TextHighlighter._renderMatches)
        let prevEnd: CharPos | null = null;

        for (const { begin, end, matchIdx } of convertedMatches) {
            // Flush tail of previous div if switching to a new one
            if (!prevEnd || begin.divIdx !== prevEnd.divIdx) {
                if (prevEnd !== null) {
                    appendTextToDiv(textDivs[prevEnd.divIdx], textContentItemsStr[prevEnd.divIdx],
                        prevEnd.offset, textContentItemsStr[prevEnd.divIdx].length);
                }
                beginDiv(textDivs[begin.divIdx], textContentItemsStr[begin.divIdx], begin.offset);
            } else {
                // Same div — fill gap between previous match end and this match start
                appendTextToDiv(textDivs[prevEnd.divIdx], textContentItemsStr[prevEnd.divIdx],
                    prevEnd.offset, begin.offset);
            }

            if (begin.divIdx === end.divIdx) {
                // Single-div match: inject inline highlight span
                const span = document.createElement('span');
                span.className = 'highlight appended';
                span.dataset.matchIndex = String(matchIdx);
                span.textContent = textContentItemsStr[begin.divIdx].substring(begin.offset, end.offset);
                textDivs[begin.divIdx].append(span);
                highlightElements.push(span);
            } else {
                // Multi-div match
                const beginSpan = document.createElement('span');
                beginSpan.className = 'highlight begin appended';
                beginSpan.dataset.matchIndex = String(matchIdx);
                beginSpan.textContent = textContentItemsStr[begin.divIdx].substring(begin.offset);
                textDivs[begin.divIdx].append(beginSpan);
                highlightElements.push(beginSpan);

                for (let n = begin.divIdx + 1; n < end.divIdx; n++) {
                    textDivs[n].className = 'highlight middle';
                    (textDivs[n] as HTMLElement).dataset.matchIndex = String(matchIdx);
                    highlightElements.push(textDivs[n]);
                }

                beginDiv(textDivs[end.divIdx], textContentItemsStr[end.divIdx], 0);
                const endSpan = document.createElement('span');
                endSpan.className = 'highlight end appended';
                endSpan.dataset.matchIndex = String(matchIdx);
                endSpan.textContent = textContentItemsStr[end.divIdx].substring(0, end.offset);
                textDivs[end.divIdx].append(endSpan);
                highlightElements.push(endSpan);
            }

            prevEnd = end;
        }

        // Flush tail of last div
        if (prevEnd !== null) {
            appendTextToDiv(textDivs[prevEnd.divIdx], textContentItemsStr[prevEnd.divIdx],
                prevEnd.offset, textContentItemsStr[prevEnd.divIdx].length);
        }
    });

    if (highlightElements.length > 0) scrollToMatch(0);
}
```

### 5. Update `scrollToMatch` (lines 166–184)

```typescript
function scrollToMatch(index: number) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.textLayer .highlight.selected')
        .forEach((el) => el.classList.remove('selected'));

    if (matchCount === 0) return;

    currentMatchIndex = ((index % matchCount) + matchCount) % matchCount;

    const currentEls = document.querySelectorAll(`[data-match-index="${currentMatchIndex}"]`);
    currentEls.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('selected'));
    currentEls[0]?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
}
```

### 6. Update CSS (lines 732–743)

Remove:
```css
:global(.search-highlight-overlay) { ... }
:global(.search-highlight-overlay.current-match) { ... }
```

Add (override pdfjs default purple highlight with conventional yellow/orange):
```css
:global(.textLayer) {
    --highlight-bg-color: rgba(255, 255, 0, 0.4);
    --highlight-selected-bg-color: rgba(255, 150, 0, 0.6);
}
```

---

## Verification

1. Run `pnpm run dev` in `packages/web`
2. Upload a PDF with proportional fonts (any typical document)
3. Search for a word that appears mid-sentence (not at line start)
4. Confirm highlight is exactly over the text, not offset to the right
5. Navigate matches with arrow buttons / Cmd+G — verify `selected` highlight color changes
6. Test multi-word search spanning text items
7. Test whole-word and case-sensitive toggles
8. Run `pnpm run lint` to confirm no TypeScript errors


If you need specific details from before exiting plan mode (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/daishokomiyama/.REDACTED.jsonl

